191 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 404 0 R/T(The key idea behind ResNets is residual learning. Instead of trying to learn the exact mapping from input to output, ResNets learn the "residual" or the difference between the input and the desired output. This makes it easier for the network to learn complex mappings and prevents degradation in performance as the network gets deeper.)/E(The key idea behind ResNets is residual learning. Instead of trying to learn the exact mapping from input to output, ResNets learn the "residual" or the difference between the input and the desired output. This makes it easier for the network to learn complex mappings and prevents degradation in performance as the network gets deeper.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

192 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 405 0 R/T(ResNet-18  has 18 layers \(17 convolutional and 1 fully connected\). This makes it faster to train and less memory intensive while still benefiting from deep feature learning.)/E(ResNet-18  has 18 layers \(17 convolutional and 1 fully connected\). This makes it faster to train and less memory intensive while still benefiting from deep feature learning.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

193 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 406 0 R/T(In medical imaging tasks, ResNet architectures, such as ResNet-18, ResNet-50, etc., are commonly used for their ability to handle complex features and learn representations from medical images effectively. )/E(In medical imaging tasks, ResNet architectures, such as ResNet-18, ResNet-50, etc., are commonly used for their ability to handle complex features and learn representations from medical images effectively. )/Pg 14 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

